{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-23T14:33:35.077Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b5b70a65052433b99eb25138","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-23T14:33:35.077Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-23T14:33:35.077Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Overlap audit: core SDK listAllComplete/certifyCompleteListResult own completeness and CLI list owns pagination. pm-context owns durable context packs and usage receipts; pm-web consumes complete SDK lists. Native pagination is pm-rust-ufzy and latency is pm-rust-wdj4. No existing embedding resource contract found. Reuse Workspace::list_page, strict decoding, lifecycle registries and JSON/TOON codecs. Add bounded private snapshot admission, cooperative cancellation and certified session receipts without another core query or parity pin. The crate remains native Rust; typed TypeScript is used for the validation harness."}]}],"before_hash":"86ac415cf8b5bf96e166c7267d2f1813f0b5c93f7e771758c759a21de12c3f44","after_hash":"e6230e2dc3a06590eb34e7ad65718412f771a3de9121f97278c6d8e46859aa4a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"588695cc9a655f01c823dd51452b42dc4150ead01a6a7cfa6d347af53eb5ecdf"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-23T14:44:13.698Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b5b70a65052433b99eb25138","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-23T14:44:13.698Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Implementation decision: immutable private disk snapshots isolate admitted reads from later writers while preserving original cursor identity. Admission accounts native working-set reserve and bounds every source read; the declared ledger ceiling is distinct from measured process RSS. Reuse canonical list_page, strict complete-item decoder and duplicate checks. Pull ownership supplies backpressure, cancellation is cooperative between copying/query boundaries, and completion/failure/cancel/drop remove snapshots. Add unchanged npm/Bun aliases for the existing Rust release gate and a Bun CI aggregate. Local work is restricted to targeted tests, lint/typecheck and focused validation because the host is saturated."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-23T14:44:13.698Z"}],"before_hash":"e6230e2dc3a06590eb34e7ad65718412f771a3de9121f97278c6d8e46859aa4a","after_hash":"7c29acde36b964c8d05d0a3cee1be33d568a2ec798b1f862949f683337daf5c1","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7938bb3299b289837309db5110b53a1579973a53ee6e75dcc81dc8adf2b81d90"}
